-- title:
--   First Switcheroo Error Le Commuting With GComplete Error
-- statement:
--   **The first switcheroo error is bounded by the complete-part commutation envelope.**
--
--   Assume $0\le\gamma\le1$, $0\le\zeta\le1$, and $d\le q$. Then the switcheroo error formed from the main commutativity error satisfies
--
--   $$
--   E_{\mathrm{sw}}\left(\zeta,\zeta;E_{\mathrm{main}}(\gamma,\zeta)\right)
--   \le
--   36m\left(\operatorname{rpow}(\gamma,1/16)+\operatorname{rpow}(\zeta,1/16)+\operatorname{rpow}(d/q,1/16)\right).
--   $$
--
--   The right-hand side is the explicit complete-part commuting-with-G error. This comparison absorbs the intermediate square-root switcheroo expression into one fractional-power envelope for use by the complete-part commutation theorem.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.firstSwitcherooError_le_commutingWithGCompleteError`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
